  "goodToKnow": "Das Osterfeuer is an Easter bonfire, lit on Holy Saturday or Easter Sunday, especially in northern Germany and the Netherlands. Villages pile up branches for weeks. It symbolises the end of winter and, in Christian terms, the light of the resurrection. Organisers must restack piles before burning so hedgehogs and birds can escape. The plural is the same."
